  "result": "I fixed it: `Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line, and all 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` matched the argument against the item's name (`l.item.name != sku`) instead of its SKU. `remove('sku-1')` compared `'sku-1'` with `'Widget'` and `'Gadget'`, found no match, and left both lines in the cart. `Cart.add` already matches on `item.sku`, so `remove` was the only place doing it differently.\n\n**Fix:** one change on that line:\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.sku != sku]\n```\n\n**Check:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, which is just the Gadget line. Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- `python3 -m unittest` ran 6 tests, all passing. (There's no `python` command here, so I used `python3`.)\n\nNone of the existing tests call `Cart.remove`, which is why this bug got through. I can add a short regression test for it if you'd like.",
